": "\\ref{lemma-exists-smooth}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{lemma-minimal-versal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-smooth-continued}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:82acbe569b7391b485a001e35bf31180d998fc698d6d8f8aea623c52e68e44e2", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:d69ae3b811b1212808c9270d6d17ec63846a02678994d540b90aa4c19eb8d31e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ae807ec610f7b98e802ba7f3675329aa4f9be2e20c4a1fd794abb8dea615521e", "source_text": "In Lemma <REF_0001> we constructed objects\n<MATH_0001> such that\n<MATH_0002> is smooth\nand such that\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nLet us reinterpret this using the theorem above. Namely,\nconsider <MATH_0003>\nas a category cofibred in groupoids over itself\n(using the identity functor).\nThen <MATH_0004> is a predeformation category,\nsatisfies (S1) and (S2), and we have <MATH_0005>.\nThus <MATH_0006> satisfies condition (3) of\nTheorem <REF_0002>.\nThe theorem implies that (2) holds, i.e.,\nwe can find a minimal versal formal object\n<MATH_0007>\nover some <MATH_0008>\nsatisfying (<REF_0003>).\nLemma <REF_0004> shows that\n<MATH_0009> is formally smooth in the <MATH_0010>-adic\ntopology (because\n<MATH_0011> is smooth).\nNow condition (<REF_0005>)\ntells us that <MATH_0012> is bijective on\n<MATH_0013>-orbits. This means the injection\n<MATH_0014> is also surjective.\nIn other words, we have\n<MATH_0015>.\nSince <MATH_0016> is formally smooth in the <MATH_0017>-adic\ntopology, we can apply More on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0006>\nto conclude the exact sequence (<REF_0007>)\nturns into a pair of identifications\n<MATHSEG_0003>and<MATHSEG_0004>\nReading the argument backwards, we find that the <MATH_0018> constructed\nin Lemma <REF_0008> carries a minimal versal object.\nBy the uniqueness of minimal versal objects\n(Lemma <REF_0009>)\nwe also conclude <MATH_0019>, i.e., the two constructions give\nthe same answer.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:008470feba380d034660467bcd11b11d5d87e57b1abdae8745d1e95c176c3648", "unit_id": "tag:06T9:statement"}
